        "id": 1778597,
        "public_url": "hackathons/hacksprint-30-karpagam-academy-of-higher-education-1778597",
        "title": "Hacksprint 3.0",
        "organization_id": 101955,
        "type": "hackathons",
        "subtype": "online_coding_challenge",
        "regn_open": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-10-27T15:06:07+05:30",
        "region": "online",
        "visibility": "public",
        "details": "<p><strong>HackSprint 3.0 &mdash; Build Bold. Ride Beyond.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>About the Event</strong></p>\n<p>HackSprint 3.0 is a national-level, 36-hour hackathon organized by the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Karpagam Academy of Higher Education (KAHE), Coimbatore, in collaboration with the Metaverse Association.</p>\n<p>HackSprint 3.0 brings together passionate developers, designers, problem-solvers, and innovators from across India to transform creative ideas into impactful, technology-driven solutions. It provides a platform to experiment with emerging technologies, collaborate with like-minded innovators, and tackle real-world challenges.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<div>Mode: Online Preliminary Round + Offline Final Round</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Final Venue: Karpagam Academy of Higher Education (KAHE), Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Final Hackathon Duration: 36 hours</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Application Deadline: 28 December 2026</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>PPT Submission Template: Will be announced soon!</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>How It Works</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Online Idea Submission &amp; Screening</strong></p>\n<p>The first round will be conducted online. Interested teams must submit a PowerPoint presentation (PPT) outlining their proposed project idea before the application deadline.</p>\n<p>The presentation should explain:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<div>Problem Statement: What real-world problem are you addressing?</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Proposed Solution: How will your idea solve the problem?</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Innovation: What makes your approach unique?</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Feasibility: How can the solution be implemented?</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Expected Impact: Who will benefit from your solution?</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Team Portfolio: Relevant projects, technical skills, and previous work, where available.</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The organizing team will evaluate submissions based on innovation, problem relevance, feasibility, technical approach, potential impact, and relevant portfolio experience.</p>\n<p>Following the evaluation, selected teams will be shortlisted for the final round.</p>\n<p>Important: Submitting an application does not guarantee participation in the final hackathon. Only shortlisted teams will be invited to the offline round.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Offline Final Hackathon</strong></p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will participate in the 36-hour offline hackathon at Karpagam Academy of Higher Education, Coimbatore.</p>\n<p>Participants will develop their proposed solutions, build prototypes, test their implementations, and present their projects to the judging panel.</p>\n<p>Final evaluation will focus on innovation, technical implementation, functionality, feasibility, problem-solving, and overall impact.</p>\n<p>Final-round dates will be announced once confirmed.</p>\n<p><strong>HackSprint 3.0 Tracks</strong></p>\n<p>1. Agrotech</p>\n<p>Leverage technology to address agricultural challenges through smart irrigation, precision farming, AI-enabled agriculture, resource optimization, and sustainable farming solutions.</p>\n<p>2. MedTech</p>\n<p>Develop technology-driven healthcare solutions focused on diagnostics, remote healthcare, medical accessibility, patient monitoring, and improved healthcare delivery.</p>\n<p>3. EduTech</p>\n<p>Reimagine education through digital learning platforms, adaptive learning systems, skill-development tools, inclusive education, and innovative teaching technologies.</p>\n<p>4. WildVisionTech</p>\n<p>Explore AI- and ML-powered solutions for wildlife conservation, anti-poaching intelligence, environmental monitoring, and biodiversity protection.</p>\n<p>5. Open Innovation</p>\n<p>Think without boundaries. Build creative, technology-driven solutions to meaningful real-world problems across any domain.</p>\n<p><strong>What Awaits You?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<div>An opportunity to showcase your creativity and technical skills.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>A platform to transform ideas into practical solutions.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Collaboration with passionate developers, designers, and innovators.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>An opportunity to present your work and receive feedback from the judging panel.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Recognition for outstanding innovation and problem-solving.</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Prize details, partners, and additional opportunities will be announced through official HackSprint 3.0 communication channels.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<div>Idea Submission: Teams must submit their project proposal as a PPT before the first-round deadline.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Screening: Teams will be shortlisted based on their ideas and relevant portfolios.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Final-Round Eligibility: Only shortlisted teams may participate in the offline final.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Originality: All submissions must comply with the originality guidelines issued by the organizers.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Project Development: Final-round participants must follow the event's development, submission, and judging guidelines.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Team Size and Eligibility: Requirements will be communicated by the organizing team through official channels.</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<div>Event Updates: Participants should follow official communications for selection results, final-round dates, and further instructions.</div>\n</li>\n</ul>",
